<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 200 mln lev 2-yr T-note issue unsold.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 200 mln lev 2-yr T-note issue unsold.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry issue of two-year floater coupon T-notes with a total par of 200 million levs was not sold after the ministry rejected the bids, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Finance Ministry did not accept the bids, and the issue is considered unsold,&quot; the BNB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance and a coupon equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 108 percent.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		 BG 2032596129</p>
<p> Par value		    200 million levs</p>
<p> Auction date		 September 13, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date		   September 19, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		September 17, 1998</p>
<p> Bids received		4.0 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	  59.78 pct of par</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
